  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to access to doulas; and to\nrepeal a chapter of the laws of 2024 amending the public health law relating\nto permitting doulas to be present in the operating room while a cesarean\nsection is being performed, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 5991-A\nand A. 7606",
    "basePrintNo": "S809",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S809-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld Chap of 2024 (as proposed in S.5991-A & A.7606); amd §2500-m, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S809\n\nSPONSOR: PERSAUD\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to access to doulas;\nand to repeal a chapter of the laws of 2024 amending the public health\nlaw relating to permitting doulas to be present in the operating room\nwhile a cesarean section is being performed, as proposed in legislative\nbills numbers S. 5991-A and A. 7606\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to L.2024, c.654, to\nclarify provisions related to allowing a birthing person access to their\ndoula and requiring all maternal healthcare facilities to post on their\nwebsite, in the facility lobbies, and in inpatient waiting areas that\nbirthing individuals have the right to access doula support.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill amends the underlying chapter to eliminate duplicative\nlanguage and align the provisions with Chapter 550 of the Laws of 2024.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 654 of the Laws of 2024. S.5991-A and\nA.7606 both passed the Senate and Assembly during the 2024 Legislative\nSession.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2024 amending the Public Health Law relating to\npermitting doulas to be present in the operating room while a cesarean\nsection is being performed, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.\n5991A and A. 7606; provided, however that section two of this act shall\ntake effect on the same date and in the same manner as a chapter of the\nlaws of 2024 amending the public health law relating to permitting\nexpecting and new mothers' access to their doulas, as proposed in legis-\nlative bills numbers S.5992-A and A.6168-A, takes effect.\n",
